      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5ae6cfc4059ed80e3a12f41c|full_name}: yes, I sure I can do that, but you seem to have missed an important word in the title: \"default\". Most users follow the default settings, which block particles up to trusted users. I'm sure there are many cases of new people wishing to start vrchat creation, only to be disappointed everyone blocks their avatar's flair by default. This change is a compromise for people who responsibly use particles, and keep them less than 500, and to stop people who try to crash others by using several thousand particles all using meshes. Encouraging new players to create content for vrchat is essential if this game wants to last another 2 or 3 years. I've talked to a few veteran users, and it seems they feel a bit burnt out putting hard work into animations, only for some people to have blocked everything.\n\nAll I'm asking is a fair compromise to make sure that new players are encouraged to take a step further beyond just stealing mmd models, or using a pre-made avatar, and come up with their own brand of creativity.\n\nSome of the funniest vrchat clips are someone who is using some sort of particle system to create something funny, and it will be a shame that those will be extinct due to the harsh safety system they have in place.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-11-12T02:42:21.252Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "I know this is already a closed case somewhere else, but hear me out. I am seeing more and more people asking for this and that particle to be disabled. The safety system has gone from people doing silly and creative things with the tools of 3D art and animation. Then, it seems a trend of particle crashers went around, where people would try to crash others with extreme particles. Instead of the soft ban of particles the safety system has put into place, could there be more effort put into the system so that instead of simply blocking all particles by default, it limits them, which has been stated to be possible by changing configs, so why would such an extreme action be taken? The same concept can be applied with worlds as well. All I ask is for a more gradient for a safety system, where anyone below known user have limited access, obviously with new users having no privileges to prevent alt account abuse.",
